{"author":{"id":"ce771b8a9b8c30a8aac165a8b1cdb0957637d3941276ec4f27335daee16d79de"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794783201,"nonce":"229CXe4+R+7uopZ3TvpxYWoCN9M=","target":"2fe2dcc787149bc66d965dafb59197e943c2d4a4864a08c631996908b39a2b84","message":"## Problem Statement\n\nOpening Leaflog lands on a marketing card and a health readout instead of a\ngrow. The environment tiles sit in a cramped auto-fill grid. There is no way\nto see how temperature, humidity, VPD, or soil moisture have moved over time —\nonly the current snapshot. The phase forecast cannot be corrected: a grower\nwho flips late, harvests early, or disagrees with the estimate has no way to\nsay so, and every recommendation silently follows the estimate. Appearance\ntraits are shown as raw code strings (`tip_burn`, `fox_tailing`) with no\nexplanation of what they mean or which way they point. Long HA entity ids\noverflow their cards on the Equipment page.\n\n## Solution\n\nThe app opens on the active grow's overview — the page that already holds the\nforecast, environment tiles, coach, and timeline. The four environment tiles\nbecome one full-width strip. The overview gains day/week/month charts for\nevery continuous reading, each drawn with a shaded band for the recommended\nrange, stepping when the grow's phase changed mid-window. The grower sets the\nphase by recording events — the same events the forecast already consumes —\nand the forecast, bands, coach, lamp advice, and day-count target all\nre-anchor from them. Photoperiod veg no longer has a silent four-week\ndefault. Appearance traits get readable labels, one-line meanings, and\ncategories; taco and canoe merge. HA entity ids wrap inside their cards.\n\n## User Stories\n\n1. As a grower, I want the app to open on my active grow's overview, so that I see my plant's state immediately without navigating.\n2. As a grower with several grows, I want the most recently updated active grow chosen automatically, so that I land where I last worked.\n3. As a grower with no active grow, I want the overview to fall back to my most recent grow, so that history stays reachable.\n4. As a new user with no grows, I want the onboarding wizard to stay the first thing I see, so that setup still guides me.\n5. As a grower, I want the environment strip to span the full container width, so that Temp, RH, VPD, and RH window use the space on wide screens.\n6. As a grower, I want the strip's tiles to stretch equally, so that the row looks balanced instead of leaving dead space.\n7. As a grower, I want day/week/month charts of temperature, humidity, and VPD, so that I can see trends instead of one snapshot.\n8. As a grower, I want charts for CO₂, soil moisture, and light, so that every continuous reading has history.\n9. As a grower, I want pH and EC shown as event points, so that my feed-entry measurements are visible over time.\n10. As a grower, I want a shaded recommended band behind each chart, so that I can see at a glance whether values are in range.\n11. As a grower, I want the band to step at phase changes inside the window, so that guidance matches what the plant needed at the time.\n12. As a grower, I want Day/Week/Month to mean the last 24 hours, 7 days, and 30 days, so that the windows reflect \"lately\", not calendar artefacts.\n13. As a grower with Home Assistant unreachable, I want charts to fall back to Leaflog's snapshot points or an explicit no-data state, so that the overview still works offline.\n14. As a grower, I want soil moisture charted against a recommended range, so that watering decisions have context.\n15. As a grower, I want that range cited and editable, so that I can trust it and tune it to my substrate.\n16. As a grower, I want to set the grow's phase myself, so that the app follows my grow rather than an estimate.\n17. As a grower, I want to backdate a phase pick, so that corrections reflect when the change really happened.\n18. As a grower, I want each phase pick to appear on the event timeline, so that the grow diary shows when and how the phase moved.\n19. As a grower, I want picking Flowering to record the flip event, so that the phase picker and the quick-add chips stay one system.\n20. As a grower, I want picking Drying to record the harvest event, so that harvest timing stays a single fact in the log.\n21. As a grower, I want the forecast to re-anchor when I record a phase event, so that the windows, bands, coach, and day-count target follow reality.\n22. As a photoperiod grower, I want veg to have no default end, so that the forecast stops pretending I flip after four weeks.\n23. As a photoperiod grower, I want to optionally plan veg weeks, so that the forecast can still project a flip when I choose to.\n24. As an autoflower grower, I want the age-based flip estimate kept, so that my forecast stays sensible without intervention.\n25. As a grower, I want appearance traits shown with readable labels and one-line meanings, so that I don't have to decode raw strings or guess what canoeing is.\n26. As a grower, I want traits grouped into categories, so that I can find the right one quickly while logging.\n27. As a grower, I want taco and canoe merged into one entry, so that I don't guess which synonym fits.\n28. As a grower, I want \"praying\" described as usually a good sign, so that a healthy plant doesn't read as a problem.\n29. As a grower, I want free-form appearance tags to keep working, so that my existing entries and custom words survive the vocabulary change.\n30. As a grower, I want phase names spelled out in the interface (\"Flowering\", not terse lowercase labels), so that it reads like a grow diary, not a database.\n31. As a grower, I want long HA entity ids to wrap inside their card, so that no value overflows the layout.\n32. As a grower, I want the full entity id on hover, so that wrapping never hides the identifier I need to verify a binding.\n33. As a grower, I want the lamp advisor to keep reacting to logged stress traits, so that advice stays grounded in my observations after the vocabulary changes.\n\n## Implementation Decisions\n\n- **Phases are events** (D073 in docs/DECISIONS.md). There is no phase\n  override state. The phase picker on the grow overview records transition\n  events: picking Flowering records a Flip, picking Drying records a Harvest,\n  and boundaries with no canonical action (into Seedling, Vegetative, Curing,\n  or back to Germination) record a new Phase-change action. For autoflowers,\n  a Flowering pick records the Phase-change variant, since Flip is\n  photoperiod semantics. Picks are backdatable and appear on the timeline.\n  The forecast's actuals gain pins for the boundaries that previously only\n  derived; flip and harvest pins already exist.\n- **No default photoperiod veg length.** A photoperiod grow stays in\n  vegetative until a pin (a flip event or Flowering pick) or a planned veg\n  length says otherwise. The silent four-week default is removed.\n  Autoflowers keep the age-based flip estimate. The forward-compression\n  behaviour of the window chain is unchanged.\n- **Landing.** The root route renders the grow overview of the most recently\n  updated grow whose status is not finished; with no active grow it falls\n  back to the most recently updated grow overall; with no grows at all the\n  onboarding wizard stays the landing view. Navigation structure unchanged.\n- **Environment strip.** The four tiles (Temp, RH, VPD, RH window) stay\n  distinct tiles in a single row that spans the full container width, each\n  tile stretching to fill; the row wraps to fewer columns on narrow screens.\n- **Charts.** New SVG charts rendered from Rust (spec §3), placed on the grow\n  overview (spec §4.11). One chart per continuous reading — temperature,\n  humidity, derived VPD, CO₂, soil moisture, light (a step series when the\n  entity is binary) — plus pH and EC from feed entries as event scatter.\n  Rolling Day / Week / Month toggles map to the last 24 hours / 7 days /\n  30 days. Watering and feed event volumes are not charted here.\n- **Bands.** Each chart draws a shaded corridor for the recommended range,\n  keyed by phase from the preset tables (VPD band, RH window, temperature\n  thresholds, and the new soil-moisture range). When the window spans a\n  pinned phase change, the corridor steps at that date. Bands are computed\n  client-side from the shared core crate; no band endpoint.\n- **History data.** One new read endpoint serves a grow's chart series per\n  sensor role and window. It merges Home Assistant's history API (via the\n  existing passthrough) with Leaflog's per-entry sensor snapshots, using a\n  pure merge function in the shared core crate so the endpoint stays a thin\n  adapter. Data is SI internally and displayed per the HA unit system. When\n  Home Assistant is unreachable the series degrades to snapshot-only points\n  or an explicit no-data state, per the Dead binding rule.\n- **Soil-moisture preset.** A new recommended range is added to the preset\n  tables: stored as a range, cited from at least two sources, user-editable\n  with reset-to-default, per the seed-data discipline in AGENTS.md.\n- **Appearance vocabulary.** Fourteen canonical traits after merging taco and\n  canoe into one \"Canoeing\" entry. Each carries a display label, a one-line\n  meaning, and a category (Overall health, Colour, Light stress,\n  Nutrient \u0026 water, Growth shape). Praying is explicitly described as\n  usually a good sign. Free-form tags stay allowed and render as typed.\n  Timeline badges use the display labels. The lamp advisor's stress\n  detection is updated to the merged vocabulary. Phase labels are spelled\n  out in the interface (\"Flowering\").\n- **Entity-id wrapping.** A shared style with wrap-anywhere behaviour plus a\n  hover title showing the unbroken id, applied to every place an HA entity\n  id renders: equipment cards, sensor-binding lists, live tiles, and the\n  onboarding sensor picker.\n- **Language.** The grow lifecycle axis stays \"Phase\"; the feed-template axis\n  stays \"Feed phase\". GLOSSARY.md now defines Grow overview, Phase pick,\n  Photoperiod, and Autoflower, with \"Dashboard\", \"grow progress\", and\n  \"stage\" on avoid-lists.\n- **Ingress and units rules are untouched.** Relative URLs everywhere; the\n  charts introduce no absolute paths. SI storage, unit-system display via\n  the existing units helpers.\n\n## Testing Decisions\n\n- Tests target external behaviour through the highest seams, not internals.\n  Two existing seams carry the weight; the only new seam is the history read\n  endpoint, and its brain is a pure core function.\n- **Core engines** (unit and property tests, prior art: the forecast engine's\n  property suite): re-anchor semantics — pins move windows, later events\n  supersede earlier picks for the boundary they describe, photoperiod veg is\n  open-ended without a pin or plan, autoflower estimates unchanged, window\n  contiguity and monotonicity invariants hold under arbitrary pins. Chart\n  series merge: window boundaries, HA-plus-snapshot merge, degradation inputs.\n  Appearance metadata: every canonical trait has a label, description, and\n  category; taco and canoe are gone; the advisor's stress detection matches\n  the merged tag; unknown free-form tags pass through.\n- **Endpoint**: thin adapter, covered through the e2e seam rather than a new\n  test layer.\n- **Playwright e2e** (prior art: the D069 suite with its native-submit marker\n  guard): landing shows the active grow's overview; the strip spans the\n  container; a chart renders line and band elements from the mock HA's\n  canned history; the phase-pick form (a real POST, so it gets the marker\n  guard) writes a timeline entry and shifts the forecast; appearance\n  checkboxes render grouped with labels; an entity id card shows no\n  horizontal overflow.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- A per-plant or per-batch harvest entity; Drying and Curing stay on the\n  grow-level phase axis, and jar inventory stays out per spec §4.14.\n- Calendar-aligned chart windows.\n- Charts of watering or feed volumes.\n- Automatic phase detection or suggestions.\n- Recommended bands for CO₂ and light (charted without bands until sourced\n  presets exist).\n- Finer VPD band splits per spec §5.2 sub-phases; the current coarser\n  mapping stays.\n- Localisation of the new strings; that belongs to the live localisation\n  effort in the tracker.\n- Everything on the v1 out-of-scope list in AGENTS.md (multi-user, cloud\n  sync, sharing, native mobile, automatic device control).\n\n## Further Notes\n\n- D073 in docs/DECISIONS.md records the phases-are-events decision and the\n  rejected override-layer alternative; the override layer lost because it\n  creates two answers to \"what phase is this grow in\" that can disagree.\n- Charts with log events overlaid as markers were already specified (§4.11)\n  but never built; this spec is that work, extended with bands and the\n  phase-event coupling.\n- New UI strings and docs must pass the prose lint (plain vocabulary, no\n  wall-of-text sentences).","files":null}]}